![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

### Defensive Row Processing and Malformed Entry Skipping

In `writeCopyFile`, properties of each `row` (such as `row.question_key`, `row.question_bank_payload`, and nested properties like `row.question_bank_payload.release_scope_status`) are accessed directly without checking if the row or its nested payloads are nullish or malformed. If any row in the projection is malformed, this will result in a runtime `TypeError` crash.

To adhere to defensive programming practices and prevent runtime property-access crashes, we should explicitly validate the row shape, skip malformed entries, and use optional chaining with safe fallbacks.

```javascript
function writeCopyFile(rows, filePath) {
  const lines = [];
  for (const row of rows) {
    if (!row || typeof row !== 'object') continue;
    const rowPosture = posture(row);
    const values = [
      row.question_key || '',
      JSON.stringify(row.question_bank_payload || {}),
      JSON.stringify(row.analysis_snapshot_payload || {}),
      JSON.stringify(row.import_receipt_payload || {}),
      rowPosture.phase_b2_mutation_eligible === true ? 'true' : 'false',
      row.question_bank_payload?.release_scope_status || '',
      rowPosture.display_posture || '',
      rowPosture.rights_display_status || '',
      rowPosture.evidence_availability_status || '',
      rowPosture.method_diagnostic_posture || '',
      JSON.stringify(sourceRefs(row) || {}),
      JSON.stringify(blockers(row) || []),
      rowHash({
        question_bank_payload: row.question_bank_payload || {},
        analysis_snapshot_payload: row.analysis_snapshot_payload || {},
        import_receipt_payload: row.import_receipt_payload || {},
      }),
    ];
    lines.push(values.map(csvCell).join('\\t'));
  }
  fs.writeFileSync(filePath, lines.join('\\n') + '\\n', 'utf8');
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When validating collections of data, explicitly check for and record malformed entries as structured validation failures, and skip further processing of those entries to avoid runtime property access errors.
</details>

